  "explanation": "The documents explicitly state that Jorge C. Romao worked at two distinct organizations. Document 1 (D1S4, D1S10) confirms his tenure at 'Oak Ridge National Laboratory' from 2007-2012. Document 2 (D2S7, D2S13) confirms he worked at 'Instituto Superior Técnico' (IST). Other candidates like the Department of Energy's Office of Science (award presenter), University of Tennessee (alma mater), and various journals/newspapers are either institutions where he studied, entities that awarded him, or media sources, not employers. The 'Materials Science and Technology Division' is a department within Oak Ridge, not a separate employer entity in this context."
